The shopkeeper gives me another shirt.
This shirt is bigger than the previous shirt.
I go into the shop's small trial room.
I try on this bigger shirt.
I look in the mirror of the trial room.
This shirt fits me perfectly.
On the shoulders, it is much better than that small shirt.
I come out of the trial room.
I say to the shopkeeper, "This size is absolutely right."
"I will take this exact shirt."
"Thank you for the easy exchange, brother."
The shopkeeper smiles and puts the shirt in the bag.
I take my bag and step out of the shop.
It is still very humid outside.
But now I have a new raincoat and the right shirt for the monsoon.
I am fully prepared for the changing weather.
I happily go back to my home by bus.
